      "emap.notready": "Story is NOT ready \u2014 {n} open question(s) must be answered first.",
      "emap.gherkin.title": "This example as a BDD scenario",
      "emap.gherkin.from": "From the example",
      "emap.bridge.bdd.title": "Open the BDD / Gherkin Explorer \u2014 green examples become executable Gherkin scenarios.",
      "emap.bridge.gates.title": "Open the Definition of Ready / Done Explorer \u2014 unresolved questions block the Definition of Ready.",
      "emap.quiz.prompt": "During example mapping, a story ends the session with several unresolved red (question) cards. What does that tell the team?",
      "emap.quiz.a": "Nothing \u2014 red cards are just decoration; pull the story into the sprint anyway.",
      "emap.quiz.b": "The story is too small; merge it with another story.",
      "emap.quiz.c": "The story is not ready \u2014 the open questions are unknowns that must be answered before it enters the sprint.",
      "emap.quiz.d": "The team wrote too many examples; delete some green cards to balance the map.",
      "emap.quiz.correct": "Correct. Red cards are unanswered questions; a story carrying them into the sprint will stall mid-flight \u2014 answer them first (this is exactly a Definition of Ready check).",
      "emap.quiz.wrong": "Not quite. Red cards are open questions \u2014 genuine unknowns. A story still carrying them is not ready; the questions must be answered before it enters the sprint.",
      "emap.lab.prompt": "Recall a story your team started with too few examples or too many open questions. What went wrong mid-sprint, and which red card \u2014 asked earlier \u2014 would have prevented it?",
