      "ctp.bridge.pyramid.title": "Open the Pyramid Adjuster \u2014 the test pyramid is exactly the suite shape that keeps the commit tier fast.",
      "ctp.bridge.flaky.title": "Open the Flaky Diagnosis Explorer \u2014 flaky tests are what erode trust in a fast pipeline.",
      "ctp.quiz.prompt": "A new end-to-end test takes 8 minutes to run. Which pipeline tier should it be assigned to?",
      "ctp.quiz.a": "The commit tier \u2014 run it on every push so failures are caught instantly.",
      "ctp.quiz.b": "The pull-request tier \u2014 8 minutes is fine to block every PR.",
      "ctp.quiz.c": "The nightly tier \u2014 an 8-minute test would wreck commit-tier feedback; run it on a slower cadence.",
      "ctp.quiz.d": "No tier \u2014 delete it; end-to-end tests are not worth running.",
      "ctp.quiz.correct": "Correct. The commit tier must stay fast (seconds, not minutes); an 8-minute test belongs on a slower tier such as nightly.",
      "ctp.quiz.wrong": "Not quite. An 8-minute test on every commit (or every PR) destroys fast feedback \u2014 and the test still has value, so do not delete it. Run it nightly.",
      "ctp.lab.prompt": "What is the slowest feedback loop in your real pipeline? Estimate how long developers wait for it, and describe one change \u2014 a faster tier, test-impact analysis, or a reshaped suite \u2014 that would shorten it.",
