            "generalFeedback": "Escaping has to be right everywhere \u2014 every input, every context, every encoding \u2014 and one overlooked path reopens the vulnerability. Parameterisation avoids the problem class by keeping the input out of the SQL string, which is why the explorer treats it as the canonical fix.",
            "single": true
