            "generalFeedback": "(x=17, y=90) passes x === 17, so approach level is 0 and cost is the normalised distance of y > 100 \u2014 a value below 1. (x=15, y=200) fails x === 17, so approach level is 1 and cost exceeds 1 regardless of y. Approach level dominates, so (17, 90) is closer.",
